# JEHMARP environment templates
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local development
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#   cp .env.local.example .env
#   npm run dev
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# GitHub Environments (staging + production)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Fill ONE file per environment and upload all secrets in a single command:
#
#   cp .env.staging.example .env.staging
#   # edit .env.staging with staging-only values
#   gh secret set --env staging -f web/.env.staging
#
#   cp .env.production.example .env.production
#   # edit .env.production with production-only values
#   gh secret set --env production -f web/.env.production
#
# Each example file includes:
#   • Worker runtime vars (Supabase, Turnstile, email, Redis, PAGE_STATUS_*)
#   • Supabase CLI secrets (ACCESS_TOKEN, PROJECT_REF, DB_PASSWORD, pooler)
#   • Cloudflare deploy secrets (API token, account id, base URL, staging KV)
#   • Smoke test credentials (SMOKE_ADMIN_*, SMOKE_AGENT_*, optional Turnstile)
#
# CI uses GitHub Environment secrets directly. During deploy, render-*-env.sh
# writes only the Worker runtime subset to .env.staging / .env.production for
# wrangler — the rest remain in GitHub for workflows only.
#
# Verify uploads:
#   gh secret list --env staging
#   gh secret list --env production
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Production Environment variables (NOT uploaded via secret -f)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Set these separately after uploading production secrets:
#
#   gh variable set CANARY_OBSERVE_SECONDS --env production --body "90"
#   gh variable set CANARY_MAX_ERROR_RATE --env production --body "0.05"
#   gh variable set VERSION_AFFINITY_REQUIRED --env production --body "false"
#   gh variable set REQUIRE_BACKUP_EVIDENCE_FOR_HIGHRISK --env production --body "false"
#   gh variable set CONTRACT_LOCK_PREFLIGHT --env production --body "true"
#   gh variable set STAGING_EVIDENCE_OPTIONAL --env production --body "false"
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secret checklist by environment
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Staging (.env.staging.example) — 40+ keys including:
#   PUBLIC_SUPABASE_*, SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY, TURNSTILE_*, RESEND_*, UPSTASH_*,
#   PAGE_STATUS_*, SUPABASE_ACCESS_TOKEN, SUPABASE_PROJECT_REF,
#   SUPABASE_DB_PASSWORD, CLOUDFLARE_*, STAGING_SESSION_KV_ID, STAGING_BASE_URL,
#   SMOKE_*
#
# Production (.env.production.example) — same app/CLI/Cloudflare/smoke keys plus:
#   PRODUCTION_BASE_URL (instead of STAGING_SESSION_KV_ID / STAGING_BASE_URL)
#
# Optional in both:
#   SUPABASE_DB_POOLER_URL, SMOKE_TURNSTILE_RESPONSE
#
# Never put LOCAL_SUPABASE_* in GitHub — local dev only (.env.local.example).
#
# Full CI/CD reference: context-factory/docs/ci-cd-plan.md
